From 6ce2ba96395a02cfb0654d11c73e425034eb7eeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:16:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Launch load: owner runs take turns at a cap of 60; an answer
 is never followed by the error line
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

From the tester's launch report (60358) after the 200-seat tests of 15 Oct.
F4: an owner's run now takes one of 60 run slots before it starts, in arrival
order, and its hard-timeout clock starts inside the slot; a waiting run keeps
the „working" status the send set, so no new text. F5: a failed run first
checks whether its own answer is already in the thread (52713 had one, then
the error line under it); if so it ends the run on the screen with that answer
and sets the status the work is in, writing no error line. The error line a
real failure owes is tried a second time when its write fails (five silent
fails in the first 200 step). Two source pins read the reindented route with
a whitespace-tolerant match.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HwFREQwL5g9E6qRrUf9bau
